## Automated checks

Run the repository's documented validation commands for generated theme colour parity, syntax and contrast. Build this documentation with `bundle exec middleman build`. Validate generated links and check that no GOV.UK crown, logotype or font assets are published.

Meaningful browser tests should cover actual behaviour: theme colour changes map to the correct available theme; native mode stays unchanged; unsupported themes do not fail silently; switching away restores the interface.

## Keyboard and screen reader

Use Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Space and arrow keys. Check the Theme colour select, native theme selector, sidebar, dialogs and representative device controls. Verify the visible label, role and state. Close a dialog and confirm focus returns to its trigger.

Check that a theme colour change is announced once and that sensor refreshes do not flood the live region. Check that unavailable and empty states are spoken in words that make sense.

## Responsive and visual checks

Check desktop, tablet and 320px phone layouts, 200% text enlargement, 400% zoom, reduced motion and forced colours. Review all seven theme colours in both modes against real text, inputs, focus, error and success states. Check light, dark and automatic preferences separately.

Inspect the supplied logo and favicon at their real sizes. Confirm that no stretched mark, clipped heading, hidden action, lost chart label or accidental page overflow appears.

## Borders, icons and attention counts

Compare structural card edges with editable fields: quiet dividers must not become ink boxes, and inputs must not inherit decorative low-contrast borders. Inspect repeated sections together, since a series of individually valid borders can still overwhelm a page. Keep keyboard focus clearly stronger than ordinary grouping.

Check the [notification badge](../components/notification-badge.html) at 0, 1, 9, 10, 98, 99 and 100 items. Verify its red rounded shape, hidden zero state, capped text, one meaningful accessible count, no extra tab stop, updates and native-theme restoration. Test surrounding backgrounds separately from white text on red.

Review shell and device icons in context: meaningful label, consistent purpose, preserved aspect ratio, sufficient contrast and a usable hit target. Confirm that a symbol is not being stretched or replaced by a missing font glyph. Native radios, switches, avatars and gauges must retain their expected geometry. Record any untested third-party icon or badge separately.

## Native Home Assistant checks

Open each route directly in a fresh session, before visiting a dashboard:

- Overview and a representative room dashboard.
- Native Energy, including date changes and data detail.
- History and charts.
- Map, including attribution and controls.
- Settings, profile, forms and a device details dialog.

Switch from civica to a different theme and back. Reload the browser and check that the preference persists. Test a slow or disconnected device, and check that missing data is not shown as zero.

## Release evidence

Record each check as passed, failed or not tested, with links to screenshots or logs where they help. Keep a separate list of unsupported third-party components. Do not count an untested item as a pass because the shared tokens are correct.
